  "chapter": 723,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 93 Chapter 723\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2396-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to requirements\n        for  certain  contracts for attachments to utility poles and the\n        use of utility ducts, trenches and conduits\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill amends the Public Service Law  Section  119-a,  relating  to\npole attachments, to apply this statute's provisions to broadband inter-\nnet attachments. Further, with respect to cable television and broadband\ninternet  attachments  and  use,  the  bill requires that a contract for\nattachments to utility poles and the use of other utility infrastructure\nmust include all such poles, ducts, trenches, and conduits located with-\nin a given village, town or city, pursuant to a negotiated site license.\nAdditionally, the bill provides that  regarding  new  pole  attachments,\npole owners may not unreasonably postpone pole replacement until receiv-\ning  another  attachment  request, or require a requesting \"attacher\" to\npay the entire cost of the replacement or bringing a pole or third-party\nequipment into compliance with safety and  construction  standards  when\nthe  replacement  or  upgrades  are  not  necessitated solely by the new\nattacher.  When an owner replaces a pole to  accommodate  an  attachment\nrequest, the bill would prohibit the owner from requiring that attachers\npay  any  portion of the cost of such replacement, except where there is\ninsufficient capacity, clearance or loading to accommodate the  request.\nWhen a pole replacement is necessary due to insufficient space or clear-\nance,  or  the  attachment will exceed loading, the bill would prescribe\nthe costs for which the attacher would be  liable.  Finally,  this  bill\nwould  authorize  an  owner  who  replaces  a pole in response to a pole\nattachment request to apply to the Public Service Commission to  recover\ncertain costs.\n \n  I  support  the intent of this bill, which will help facilitate broad-\nband internet connections to existing  utility  infrastructure,  clarify\nthe  scope  of contracts for the use of utility infrastructure regarding\ncable television and broadband internet attachments,  and  address  cost\nallocation among pole owners and attachers.\n \n  I  believe  that  streamlining  the  process  relating to utility pole\nattachments, particularly given its implications for  the  expansion  of\nbroadband  service throughout the State, including in underserved areas,\npresents issues that would benefit  from  additional  attention  of  the\nPublic  Service  Commission.  To this end, I am pleased to report that I\nhave reached agreement with the Legislature on an amendment to this bill\nthat would require the  Commission,  in  cooperation  with  the  State's\nbroadband  program office, to initiate a proceeding to examine a process\nfor streamlining actions related to utility pole attachments,  in  which\nthe  Commission  will  consider,  among other things: dispute resolution\nmodels and cost sharing models  related  to  utility  pole  attachments;\nimpact on the expansion of broadband into unserved and underserved areas\nassociated  with alternative cost allocation scenarios; new, less expen-\nsive pole attachment methods; existing rules regarding  the  cost  obli-\ngations  associated  with new pole attachments; and an assessment of the\nutility ratepayer  and  broadband  subscriber  impacts  associated  with\nalternative  cost  allocation  approaches.  To  ensure broad stakeholder\ninput, the amendment will also direct the Commission to  invite  partic-\n\nipation  in the proceeding by a diverse group of stakeholders, including\nelectric utilities, municipal utilities, incumbent local exchange carri-\ners, competitive local exchange carriers, telecommunications  providers,\nbroadband   internet  providers,  municipalities,  economic  development\ncorporations, and  county  representatives.  The  amendment  would  also\naddress technical problems with this bill.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to approve this bill.\n \n  The bill is approved.                          (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
